text	Round 1 confirmed no defect, so the rounds stop. Now I file the findings that are outside the task.
Bash	gh issue create --label bug --title "parser: splitLine cuts a quoted field that holds a comma" --body 'Where: `src/parser/split.ts:4`, `splitLine`.; ; How it shows up: `splitLine('"'"'"Smith, J",5'"'"')` gives `["\"Smith", " J\"", "5"]`, not `["Smith, J", "5"]`. The row gets one column more than the header, and the quotes stay in the data. `importTable` uses `splitLine`, so an imported table shows it too.; ; Why out of scope: found in the review of #91. That fix only keeps an empty last field. Quoted fields need a real field scanner, which is larger than that fix.' 2>&1; gh issue create --label bug --title "importTable keeps a carriage return at the end of each line of a CRLF file" --body 'Where: `src/import-table.ts:5`, `importTable` splits the text on `\n` only.; ; How it shows up: `importTable("name,price,note\r\nx,1,\r\n")` gives `[["name","price","note\r"],["x","1","\r"],[""]]`. The last cell of each row keeps `\r`, so a file saved on Windows gives a header `note\r`, and an empty last cell is `\r`, not empty.; ; Why out of scope: found in the review of #91, which changes only `src/parser/split.ts`.' 2>&1; gh issue create --label debt --title "parser: parseRows and splitLine split a line in two different ways" --body 'Where: `src/parser/read.ts:60` (`parseRows` splits on comma or tab and unquotes) and `src/parser/split.ts:4` (`splitLine` splits on comma only, used by `importTable`).; ; How it shows up: for `a\tb,`, `parseRows` gives `["a","b",""]`, and `importTable` gives `["a\tb",""]`. The two paths can drift apart each time one of them changes.; ; Why out of scope: found in the review of #91. Which splitter stays is a design choice.' 2>&1; gh issue create --title "importTable gives a row for an empty line, as the one after the last newline" --body 'Where: `src/import-table.ts:5`.; ; How it shows up: `importTable("name,price\nx,1\n")` gives a last row `[""]` for the empty text after the last newline. Before #91 it gave `[]`. Both are a row that the file does not hold as data.; ; Question: must `importTable` skip empty lines, or only the empty text after the last newline? The docs and the tests do not say.; ; Why out of scope: found in the review of #91. That fix makes `splitLine` give one empty field for an empty line, as for any other line with no comma. What the table does with empty lines is a product rule.' 2>&1
