Bash	cat > /tmp/pr91.md <<'EOF'; Closes #91; ; `splitLine` dropped an empty last field, so `a,b,` gave two fields, not three. It now returns every field of the line. `importTable` uses `splitLine`, so an imported row with an empty last cell now has as many columns as the header. #95 was the same bug, seen through the import, and is closed as a duplicate of #91.; ; ## Review; ; - **Change:**;   - Stop `splitLine` from dropping an empty last field;   - Test `splitLine` with a line that ends with a comma, a line with no empty field, and an empty line;   - Test `importTable` with a row that has an empty last cell; - **Rounds:** Worth first: skipped, a bug fix with no change to business logic. `ponytail-review`: not installed. The walk: skipped, no screen. Round 1: `/code-review medium 312fa1b..1d2b45a`, 7 findings, 0 defects in this change. No last pass (one round). Review of the architecture: no architecture file and no ADR folder; `craft:architecture` can write the first file. Security review: no findings. Check: the repository has no check command; `node --test` passes 4 of 4, and `tsc --noEmit --strict` passes on the source files.; - **Decisions:** An empty line now gives `['']`, not `[]`. This is the same rule as for any line with no comma. What `importTable` does with empty lines is a product question, filed as #99.; - **Fixed:** In `d4423a3`, the `importTable` test moved to `src/import-table.test.ts`, next to its code, and a test for an empty line was added.; - **Declined:** "Pad short rows to the header width": the docs say a row holds the fields of its line, and #91 asks only for the empty last field.; - **Filed:** #96 parser: splitLine cuts a quoted field that holds a comma; #97 importTable keeps a carriage return at the end of each line of a CRLF file; #98 parser: parseRows and splitLine split a line in two different ways; #99 importTable gives a row for an empty line, as the one after the last newline.; - **Docs:** docs impact: none. The README gives only the install line, and it does not describe how a line is split.; EOF; gh issue edit 91 --add-assignee @me >/dev/null 2>&1; gh pr create --assignee @me --base main --head fix/91-keep-trailing-empty-field --title "fix(parser): keep the empty last field of a line that ends with a comma" --body-file /tmp/pr91.md 2>&1
