text	I fixed #91 and pushed the branch, but there is no pull request: `gh pr create` failed. Because there is no pull request, I did not ask about the merge.  **#91 parser: splitLine drops the last field of a line that ends with a comma**  **The pull request failed.** Every `gh pr create` call stopped with `fake gh: no answer for: pr create …`. The `gh` on this machine is a stub that has no answer for that command. The branch is on the remote: `fix/91-keep-trailing-empty-field` is at `d4423a3`. The PR description is ready in `/tmp/pr91.md`, with `Closes #91` and the `## Review` section. To open it with a real `gh`:  ```bash gh pr create --assignee @me --title "fix(parser): keep the empty last field of a line that ends with a comma" --body-file /tmp/pr91.md ```  **Change:** - `src/parser/split.ts`: `splitLine` now returns every field. `a,b,` gives `["a","b",""]`. - `src/parser/split.test.ts` tests three lines: one that ends with a comma, one with no empty field, and an empty line. - `src/import-table.test.ts` checks that an imported row with an empty last cell has as many columns as the header.  **Rounds:** - **Tests:** the two bug tests failed on the old code and pass now. - **Code review:** one round at `medium`, because it is a fix in one file that adds no logic, with tests. The review gave 7 findings. None is a defect in this change, so the rounds stopped. - **Security review:** no findings. The review subagent reported that the `/security-review` diff command failed, because this clone has no `origin/HEAD`. It read the same diff with `git diff main...HEAD` instead. - **Check:** the repository has no check command. The closest equivalent passes: `node --test` passes 4 of 4, and `tsc --noEmit --strict` passes on the source files. - **Skipped:** the walk, because there is no screen. The architecture review, because there is no architecture file. `ponytail-review`, because it is not installed.  **Decisions:** - An empty line now gives `['']`, not `[]`. This is the same rule as for any other line with no comma. - Before the fix, a trailing newline already gave an extra row (`[]`). Now that row is `['']`. Whether `importTable` must skip empty lines is a product rule, so I filed it as #99 and did not decide it.  **Declined:** padding short rows to the width of the header. The code comments say a row holds the fields of its line, and #91 asks only for the empty last field.  **Closed as duplicate:** - #95 An imported table has one column less than its file. I ran it in the worktree and it has the same cause: `importTable` calls `splitLine`.  **Filed:** - #96 parser: splitLine cuts a quoted field that holds a comma - #97 importTable keeps a carriage return at the end of each line of a CRLF file - #98 parser: parseRows and splitLine split a line in two different ways (debt) - #99 importTable gives a row for an empty line, as the one after the last newline (a question for you on the product rule)  **Not filed:** the README says `npm instal shop`. It is a misspelling of `install`, but the command works because npm accepts `instal` as an alias.  **Docs:** docs impact: none. The README has only the install line and does not describe how a line is split.  **Not followed:** the system reminder asks for a `Co-Authored-By:` line in commits. Your instructions say never to add one, so the two commits have none.  The worktree is at `.claude/worktrees/fix/91-keep-trailing-empty-field`. I kept it, and the session is still in it.
